<isscript>
    var configHelper = require('*/cartridge/scripts/personalization/configHelper');
    var psConfig = configHelper.getConfig();
    // Only gated on the enable/disable switch here — the Personalization decision call has
    // no dependency on the SCAPI hydration fields, so this doesn't require those to be set.
    var psEnabled = psConfig.enabled;
    var psPointName = configHelper.resolvePointName('sfra', pdict.contextKey, pdict.personalizationPointName);
    var psCarouselId = 'ps-carousel-' + (pdict.contextKey || 'default');
    // Which tile-rendering strategy this zone uses — set by the slot template that includes
    // this file (see slots/personalization/{home,cart}.isml and their -sfra variants).
    // Whitelisted rather than trusted verbatim so a bad/missing value can never break rendering.
    var psRenderMode = (pdict.renderMode === 'sfra') ? 'sfra' : 'scapi';
    // Origin-only (scheme+host[:port]), for the preconnect resource hints below — dcSdkUrl and
    // shortCode are known at render time regardless of render mode, so the connection to
    // whichever cross-origin host this zone will call can be warmed up before any JS has run.
    var originMatch = psConfig.dcSdkUrl && psConfig.dcSdkUrl.match(/^https?:\/\/[^/]+/);
    var psDcSdkOrigin = originMatch ? originMatch[0] : null;
    var psScapiOrigin = psConfig.shortCode ? 'https://' + psConfig.shortCode + '.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com' : null;
</isscript>

<isif condition="${psEnabled}">
    <div class="ps-zone" data-ps-point="${psPointName}" data-ps-context="${pdict.contextKey || ''}" data-ps-render-mode="${psRenderMode}">
        <iscomment>
            Preconnect resource hints: warms up the TLS handshake to the Data Cloud SDK CDN and/or
            the SCAPI shopper-products domain while the rest of the page is still loading, so the
            deferred script's actual requests (fired later, at DOMContentLoaded) don't also pay for
            connection setup. The SCAPI domain uses crossorigin because fetchLiveProductData() calls
            it via fetch() with an Authorization header (a CORS request); the SDK domain doesn't,
            since it's loaded via a plain &lt;script src&gt; tag, same as any third-party script.
        </iscomment>
        <isif condition="${psDcSdkOrigin}">
            <link rel="preconnect" href="${psDcSdkOrigin}" />
        </isif>
        <isif condition="${psScapiOrigin}">
            <link rel="preconnect" href="${psScapiOrigin}" crossorigin="anonymous" />
        </isif>

        <iscomment>
            assets.addCss/addJs won't work here: this template renders inside a Content Slot,
            deep in the page body, well after common/layout/htmlHead already printed the page head —
            so anything registered this late never makes it onto the page. carousel.js is loaded
            inline below (same as personalizationTiles.js); carousel.css is injected into the page
            head client-side by personalizationTiles.js for the same reason.
        </iscomment>
        <script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/js/carousel.js')}"></script>
        <script>
            window.psCarouselCssUrl = '${URLUtils.staticURL('/css/experience/components/commerceLayouts/carousel.css')}';
        </script>

        <iscomment>
            Inlined (not client-injected like carousel.css above) because it has to paint on first
            render, before personalizationTiles.js has even downloaded — that's the whole point of
            a loading placeholder. It only styles .ps-skeleton-* elements, so it can't conflict with
            carousel.css/row-layout CSS which arrive later and restyle .carousel-item/.carousel-inner.
        </iscomment>
        <style>
            .ps-skeleton-row { display: flex; gap: 1rem; overflow: hidden; position: relative; width: 100%; min-height: 260px; padding: 0.5rem 0; }
            .ps-skeleton-tile { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 220px; }
            .ps-skeleton-image, .ps-skeleton-line { border-radius: 4px; background: #e9e9e9; background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #e9e9e9 0px, #f6f6f6 40px, #e9e9e9 80px); background-size: 600px; animation: ps-skeleton-shimmer 1.4s ease-in-out infinite; }
            .ps-skeleton-image { width: 100%; height: 220px; }
            .ps-skeleton-line { height: 14px; margin-top: 10px; }
            .ps-skeleton-line-title { width: 80%; }
            .ps-skeleton-line-price { width: 40%; }
            @keyframes ps-skeleton-shimmer { 0% { background-position: -600px 0; } 100% { background-position: 600px 0; } }
            .ps-skeleton-spinner-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
            .ps-skeleton-spinner { width: 32px; height: 32px; border: 3px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15); border-top-color: #0176d3; border-radius: 50%; animation: ps-skeleton-spin 0.8s linear infinite; }
            @keyframes ps-skeleton-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
            @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
                .ps-skeleton-image, .ps-skeleton-line, .ps-skeleton-spinner { animation: none; }
            }
        </style>

        <h3 class="ps-zone-title">${pdict.title || Resource.msg('ps.recommendations.title', 'personalization', null)}</h3>

        <div class="experience-commerce_layouts-carousel">
            <iscomment>
                Carousel shell is rendered server-side (empty) so app_storefront_base's carousel.js
                touch-swipe/accessibility bindings — which run once at document-ready against
                whatever .carousel elements already exist — pick this one up. Tiles are injected
                into .carousel-inner client-side once the Personalization decision resolves (same
                async-fill pattern as einsteinCarousel.js's fillDomElement).
            </iscomment>
            <div class="carousel slide carousel-sm-2 carousel-md-4" id="${psCarouselId}"
                 data-keyboard="true" data-interval="false"
                 data-xs="1" data-sm="2" data-md="4" data-number-of-slides="0"
                 data-ps-carousel>
                <div class="carousel-inner" data-ps-tile-row aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
                    <iscomment>
                        Skeleton placeholder: shown immediately on first paint, before any JS has run.
                        renderZone()/renderSfraZone() in personalizationTiles.js all set
                        row.innerHTML = '' before appending real tiles, so this is cleared
                        automatically once hydration completes — no extra JS needed.
                    </iscomment>
                    <div class="ps-skeleton-row" data-ps-skeleton aria-hidden="true">
                        <iscomment>4 placeholder tiles, matching the data-md="4" desktop visible count above.</iscomment>
                        <isloop begin="0" end="3" var="i">
                            <div class="ps-skeleton-tile">
                                <div class="ps-skeleton-image"></div>
                                <div class="ps-skeleton-line ps-skeleton-line-title"></div>
                                <div class="ps-skeleton-line ps-skeleton-line-price"></div>
                            </div>
                        </isloop>
                        <div class="ps-skeleton-spinner-overlay">
                            <div class="ps-skeleton-spinner"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <ol class="pd-carousel-indicators" data-ps-indicators></ol>
                <a class="carousel-control-prev" href="${'#' + psCarouselId}" role="button" data-slide="prev">
                    <span class="carousel-control-prev-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="sr-only">${Resource.msg('ps.carousel.previous', 'personalization', null)}</span>
                </a>
                <a class="carousel-control-next" href="${'#' + psCarouselId}" role="button" data-slide="next">
                    <span class="carousel-control-next-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="sr-only">${Resource.msg('ps.carousel.next', 'personalization', null)}</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <iscomment>
            Reuses the storefront's existing product-tile markup/classes so hydrated tiles inherit
            the same CSS and caching as tiles rendered elsewhere on the site (per the "leverage
            existing cached components" requirement). Adjust the selectors below to match this
            storefront's actual .product-tile markup before shipping.
        </iscomment>
        <template id="ps-tile-template" data-ps-tile-template>
            <div class="product product-tile ps-tile-template" data-pid="">
                <div class="image-container">
                    <a data-ps-field="link" href="#">
                        <img data-ps-field="image" class="tile-image" src="" alt="" />
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div class="tile-body">
                    <a data-ps-field="link" href="#">
                        <span data-ps-field="name" class="pdp-link"></span>
                    </a>
                    <div class="price" data-ps-field="priceContainer">
                        <span data-ps-field="price"></span>
                    </div>
                    <div data-ps-field="promo" class="promotion-message" hidden></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </template>
    </div>

    <script>
        window.psConfigUrl = '${URLUtils.url('PersonalizationTiles-GetConfig')}';
    </script>
    <iscomment>
        ps_dcSdkUrl is a static site preference (see configHelper.getConfig above) -- the same
        value GetConfig's JSON would return, just read here instead so the SDK script load below
        can start immediately instead of waiting on the GetConfig round-trip to learn it.
    </iscomment>
    <script>
        window.psDcSdkUrl = '${psConfig.dcSdkUrl}';
    </script>
    <iscomment>
        defer (not async) on the script tag below: keeps it from blocking HTML parsing and
        DOMContentLoaded the way a plain script tag with no attribute would, without racing the
        DOMContentLoaded listener further down -- deferred scripts are guaranteed to finish
        executing (so window.psInitTiles is defined) before DOMContentLoaded fires, unlike async,
        which offers no such ordering guarantee.
    </iscomment>
    <script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/js/personalizationTiles.js')}" defer="defer"></script>
    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
            if (window.psInitTiles) {
                window.psInitTiles(window.psConfigUrl, window.psDcSdkUrl);
            }
        });
    </script>
</isif>
